{
  "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
  "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher, Esq., on behalf of the Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I just want to read to you the operative language of Section 3553(e). It says: \"Such sentence shall be imposed in accordance with the guidelines and policy statements issued by the Sentencing Commission pursuant to section 994.\" So, in other words, that text directs the court straight to the guidelines, not away from the guidelines."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: The problem really is that the guidelines are a little confusing. They talk about an initial guidelines range, and then they tell the court that the real guideline range is a statutory minimum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners' brief",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0000-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\"Such sentence shall be imposed in accordance with the guidelines and policy statements issued by the Sentencing Commission pursuant to section 994.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What if the district judge specifically disavows any reliance on the guidelines? What if the district judge says I don't care if the guidelines are subsequently lowered; this is the sentence I'm imposing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners' argument",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what the Court said is that -- and I think what the plain text directs -- is that the mandatory minimum is set aside when the substantial assistance motion is granted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, then -- then what effect does the next sentence have?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, why -- why is that, Mr. Feigin? I -- I mean, this language speaks in terms of questions of historical fact. It's what you were sentenced based on, not what you were sentenced -- you know, what -- what your sentence should have been based on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I guess I don't quite understand that just as a matter of language,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: Well, Your Honor, here, I think \"based on a sentencing range\" actually has a very specific meaning. As we point out in the first section of our brief and as Petitioners never really respond to in their reply brief, \"sentencing range\" is a term that's only used in three different places in the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They don't claim that the Commission could write a rule that says everyone who is sentenced to a 20-year statutory minimum under 21 U.S.C. 841 now gets a 10-year sentence. Instead, to the extent they're relying on the ability of the Commission or the judge to recommend or impose a sentence that is below the statutory minimum, they're relying on Section 3553(e)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5716",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "144755bc18ca244c9041cb0ca5ee40e0c8146aeec7f6c96e9217b8325de75bb8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-144755bc18ca-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:05 p.m., the hearing concluded.)"
    },
